###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training times per configuration are in Table 1 (10 to 432 min). MD time
# per step on 32 CPU cores and one A100 (Table 2): SchNet 6 ms, PaiNN 11,
# NequIP 18, Allegro 12 and MACE 66 ms for the 149-atom cluster, against
# about 20 s per AIMD step on 64 cores and eight A100s. The MD runs used
# the lowest-MAE model of each architecture; the timings are linked to
# that model where it is unique (SchNet, PaiNN, NequIP).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table 1 reports force MAEs only; energy errors are not tabulated. The timed models are 'the single model exhibiting the lowest force MAE' per architecture; Allegro has several configurations at 12 meV/A and the timed MACE model was refined by active learning, so these two timings are not placed on a result.
# - Learning rates are 1e-3 for MACE, NequIP and Allegro and 1e-4 for SchNet and PaiNN; radial-basis settings (40 RBFs for SchNet and MACE, 10 Bessel functions for NequIP and Allegro) are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/usman2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

